{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/990397-revenants-playing-as-one","id":990397,"title":"Revenants: Playing as one.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-20T07:13:39-07:00","id":990397,"title":"Revenants: Playing as one.","content":"Hello everyone! Long time lurker, first time poster <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'll start by providing a little background about my specific situation. I'm playing a 2nd edition Requiem campaign and my character is in a unique position. The other four players are a Mekhet, a Gangrel, a Ventrue, and a Daeva. I, however, do to odd joining circumstances, am playing a Ghoul. This has worked out pretty awesome so far, as my regent is also the sire of one of the other PCs.<br /> <br /> Now, things look like they're about to go completely sideways for everyone, and there's an almost certain chance my character will die. My GM and I have decided that when that happens, my character can come back as a revenant. I've looked through the Blood &amp; Smoke book and read everything about revenants, but it's bare.<br /> <br /> Which leads to my question: What else should I take into account when it comes to role playing this? The rules are pretty basic, and it doesn't seem too hard to swing there, but the fluff is pretty sparse, mostly talking about revenants from the perspective of horrible accidents and problems of regular kindred. Not really anything on what it's like from the revenant\u2019s point of view.<br /> <br /> So yeah! Any commentary would be super appreciated! Even for a GMing perspective, because I know my GM is lurking around here somewhere <i>(Hi!)</i> and she\u2019ll probably find this thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12572-electrographic","name":"Electrographic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T07:26:58-07:00","id":990401,"title":"","content":"I think you should be prepared that one of the other players may want to &quot;finish&quot; your Embrace. That's something they can do, and with a Revenant's dietary issues and waking up every night in a frenzy they might decide that's better than letting you run around &quot;Clanless&quot;.<br /> <br /> From a Revenant's point of view, I imagine things are pretty bleak: you have basically the same drawbacks as a vampire, plus a few others (feeding while in a Frenzy almost definitely means you'll kill your target, which means Humanity checks: yay Beats!) and few of the strengths. Perhaps you'd ask your regnant to complete your Embrace since you already trust/are Blood Bound to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T07:31:28-07:00","id":990403,"title":"","content":"Alternately if you have a torpid enemy vampire handy you can use them to uplift yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T08:04:03-07:00","id":990412,"title":"","content":"Have you checked out the Neglatu? They're a Revenant-specific Bloodline, and their writeup is from a PC perspective. If nothing else, it might give you some insight as to what a PC Revenant might look like.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/lonely-together/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/lonely-together/\" target=\"_blank\"> Lonely Together &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/lonely-together/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/lonely-together/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T21:32:12-07:00","id":990787,"title":"","content":"Thank you all for your replies!<br /> <br /> Knowing the other PCs, there is a pretty good chance someone might uplift my ghoul-turned-revenant, or his regent <i>miiiight,</i> provided she doesn't get offed when things blow up LOL. Still, those are really good points about the frenzies though. Somehow my ghoul's managed to get to Integrity 8 so I think he's gonna take accidentally killing people pretty bad (Which is more fun!). He's probably not gonna find any torpid vampires himself, but that's a fun note to mention to my GM.<br /> <br /> I haven't looked to hard at bloodlines before, so I hadn't heard of the Neglatu. It was a really cool read, so thank you for bringing it up!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12572-electrographic","name":"Electrographic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T00:45:37-07:00","id":990839,"title":"","content":"The Onyx Path has a book planned called Half Damned for Reverants, Ghoul, and Dampyr PCs for the VtR setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T12:46:38-07:00","id":991072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/990397-revenants-playing-as-one?p=990839#post990839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Onyx Path has a book planned called Half Damned for Reverants, Ghoul, and Dampyr PCs for the VtR setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but don't put your chronicle on hold waiting for it. You could be waiting a long time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T13:32:51-07:00","id":991087,"title":"","content":"Hey there Elecrtographic, welcome to the forums proper. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I actually played a Revenent for a brief stint in a Chronicle before he was properly Embraced by one of the other Player Characters. Here are some of the big points that stuck out for me:<br /> <br /> 1. A Revenent's blood sympathy with their accidental creator is stupid powerful, for my character it constantly pulled at his psyche and gave him vision. In the context of my character he didn't even really know what he was, so the vision became sort of a lifeline. For your's it depends since they were a Ghoul before they arose, so how they view the call is entirely up to you and the storyteller.<br /> <br /> 2. No Vampire player has known hunger until they play a Revenent. It seems bad on paper waking up with 0 Vitae each night, but playing through that is absolutely brutal. There's a reason Revenents are usually just destroyed when discovered, and that reason is because unless they have friends who can supply blood immediately upon waking they will almost certainly frenzy at the nearest source of Vitae.<br /> <br /> 3. This is just how I played it but to me unlike the other Kindred, Revenants don't have a solid Beast to torment their psyche. All of the other players slowly developed their own Beast to match their Clan, Covenant, or personality, but for the Revenant I always played it as just a hungry void that only sought to be filled/completed. It wasn't until he was properly Embraced as a Gangrel that a form emerged from the void as his Beast. This isn't cannon, but I played it up to great effect. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T15:28:30-07:00","id":991149,"title":"","content":"I'll probably check out that book when it comes out, but yeah, we're not holing up the campaign for it. We're actually playing tonight, but I don't think he'll die until the end of the session.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the welcome, Dusksage! This is all really awesome advice. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> On #1, that's really good to keep in mind, because I think most of what my ghoul knows is through observation and a need to know basis, so he's not gonna know what's up, and he'll have just shaken off a level 3 blood bond. Not sure any of the other PCs know about revenants either, so that'll be super fun.<br /> <br /> #2, This actually sounds a lot like playing the &quot;Ghoul&quot; skin from the game Monsterhearts, since they're also prone to completely losing it and killing people to consume. Hilariously, my character might end up with the lowest humanity after this from offing to many people by accident.<br /> <br /> #3, I really like this approach to the beast, and it's kinda how my GM has been running it for kindred proper, so I'm definitely telling her about that part! I also find it fun that your character got embraced Gangrel, since my odds are best of getting that too LOL","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12572-electrographic","name":"Electrographic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T15:08:56-07:00","id":996288,"title":"","content":"I'm am currently GMing a chronicle where the players just got out of a two part prologue. The first part was as mortals until their got exanguinated and the second part was actually about them digging themselves out of the ground and finding out what they were. They were actually revenants and had to understand they needed to find their maker to be uplifted as true kindred. It was rough for them and it served as a tremendous introduction to what being a vampire is. Essentially, the focus is so much on finding blood and dealing with the mess they leave behind that it turns into a more extreme version of what being a vampire is. Even after they get uplifted, it resonates with them and serves as a reminder of what they are. Moreover, they still need to deal with the attention they drove to themselves as revenants because of the extreme feeding regimen.<br /> <br /> It's not something that is sustainable long term, mind you, but playing a revenant really gives that vampiric feel to the chronicle and helps set the tone. I think once the revenant knows he can be uplifted, that should be the one thing driving him because he knows it's only a matter of time before he gets destroyed if he doesn't find a way. Roleplaying the feeling of urgency and the despair that goes with it is fun and critical to interpreting what being a revenant is. There is no peace of mind and a character may set aside his personal values as necessity takes priority. Even after being uplifted, his time as a revenant should be a pillar in defining the true kindred the PC has become.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12610,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12610-lestat","user":"Lestat","date":". 11-01-2016, 08:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12610-lestat","name":"Lestat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12610_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T14:10:02-07:00","id":996794,"title":"","content":"I played as a revenant in my last chronicle, and found it to be a lot of fun at the start, then got pretty tiresome by the time I convinced someone to uplift me. I mean, you earn buttloads of XP because it's Vampire cranked up to 11, but you will leave a trail of dead bodies behind and your Humanity will nosedive.<br /> <br /> I can semi-recommend it, but I don't think I'd want to go through it all again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/231-blitzburger","name":"Blitzburger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar231_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T15:46:22-07:00","id":996850,"title":"","content":"Well, if you like playing doormats, I guess a revenant is an option. Unless the GM is being nice, it sounds like hell. You're running low on blood all the time and have a pretty good chance of frenzying every night. At best, vampires facepalm when they hear about you, at worst, they decide you're too much of a bother to let live. Your only hope of improving your situation is vampires, the characters known to be the prototypical selfish petty douchebags of the roleplaying universe since the 90s. So, then unless you're really lucky and find a vampire who pities you enough (or feels lonely enough, which might not be so lucky) to sacrifice a humanity dot on your sorry ass, chances are you'll end up being embraced by some asshole who sees an easy cult member/gimp or led around doing some other asshole's dirty work for fre- I mean for the promise of a full embrace when you've repaid your future debt, one day, maybe. And of course, &quot;improving&quot; your situation means getting thrown into vampire society.<br /> <br /> Seriously, playing a revenant sounds like the player/GM equivalent of an S&amp;M relationship. Well. Even more than regular player/GM relationships.<br /> <br /> But that said, a revenant who not only stayed a revenant for some time and didn't just kill himself or slipped and got destroyed, but stayed determined enough to eventually find a vampire to finish the job sounds like they would have the strength of character (or trauma) to make the kind of kindred you don't want to mess with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T03:25:42-07:00","id":997067,"title":"","content":"Or you could just eat them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T07:51:33-07:00","id":997137,"title":"","content":"Honestly I feel like Revenants that actually last some time would be pretty terrifying. This would be a vampire who can't afford to lose ever, and they'll always be struggling for their next meal. That combination resembles wet dynamite, in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T14:13:21-07:00","id":997359,"title":"","content":"Revenants arent burned by the Sun (Yay Blood Potency 0) Something to be said for it I guess","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T14:16:08-07:00","id":997362,"title":"","content":"Revenants are considered to have blood potency 1 for the most part. They burn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T19:57:38-07:00","id":997518,"title":"","content":"More thanks for all your responses, I love hearing all these different perspectives! Lots of notes for the idea bank! I actually imagine my character won't be a revenant for the rest of the campaign, but just another chapter in a long downward spiral LOL. It's fascinating to hear all the different ways people have found to get uplifted or dealt with extended time as a revenant. It's a very brutal experience, all things considered.<br /> <br /> S. Brechen mentioned the being a doormat and stuck at the whims of a GM. I definitely get those concerns, and I would be super careful who I'd play this scenario with. It could easily be go south, so it's not for every campaign, group, or player. Luckily, my GM is really cool, so I'm not afraid of getting kicked around too much because she'll work with me if things get unfun. As for the doormat issue, in general, yeah, not too fun, but my character in particular is a Ghoul. Specifically the only Ghoul surrounded by neonates (the rest of the PCs). It's been a pretty unique experience already, and he's been alternatively pushed around, toyed with, been been collateral damage in an Ordo Dracul initiation, etc. so becoming a revenant might actually be an upgrade for him LOL.<br /> <br /> And just for a little update, he died last session (he took an axe to head). We're gonna play in a few days, and he'll come back then, so I'll update with how that goes! I'm 99.98% sure he's going to kill someone in a frenzy first thing =D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12572-electrographic","name":"Electrographic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T22:27:41-07:00","id":997557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/990397-revenants-playing-as-one?p=997359#post997359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Revenants arent burned by the Sun (Yay Blood Potency 0) Something to be said for it I guess</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually, revenants still count as Blood Potency 1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T23:59:12-07:00","id":997581,"title":"","content":"Is not a difficult thing to houserule though, to at least give them some silver lining.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T12:39:54-07:00","id":998388,"title":"","content":"So, I'm the original poster's GM, and our game is tonight!<br /> <br /> My question would be if her revenant would get the free Discipline and Merit dots that you usually get when becoming a Vampire, or if those would wait until the revenant is raised up into a clan? My reading of the rules is leaning toward the latter option, but I wanted to be sure. Since he's a ghoul, I'd assume he'd keep the Disciplines he already knows as well.<br /> <br /> And just as an fyi, my main goal is for my players to have fun, so this revenant saga will go on as long as it's fun for my player. If it no longer becomes fun for her and her character hasn't been raised into a Clan by the other PCs by that point, I'll send in an NPC to do the job.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4497-tellme_tellme","name":"TellMe_TellMe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4497_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T12:59:09-07:00","id":998401,"title":"","content":"Well, revenants learn disciplines as out of clan, so I'd say it wouldn't be absurd for him to get no automatic disciplines, especially if he already knows a couple, being a ghoul. Then, once a vampire uplifts him, he'll get his free dots.<br /> <br /> You can start that way at least. If it becomes a bit burdensome and he's really in need of more discipline, maybe you could be nice. I mean, he probably has sort of an idea what clan he wants, so you could give him maybe one dot of the disciplines of that clan, maybe barring the clan specific one (dominate, auspex, etc.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T10:24:48-08:00","id":999296,"title":"","content":"Here's a little update on what we did and how it went during the first night back. We broke down what my revenant could get into two parts, so he'd get most of the vampire template, but not anything clan specific unless/until he got uplifted.<br /> <br /> Pre-Uplift<br /> - 3 Merit Points<br /> - Mask<br /> - Dirge<br /> - Touchstone<br /> - 1 Out of Clan Discipline Dot (No Specialty)<br /> - Blood Potency 1<br /> <br /> Post-Uplift<br /> - 2 In-Clan Disciplines<br /> - 1 attribute dot<br /> <br /> Since he had drank from a Gangrel and a Daeva, he was allowed to choose from any of their nonspecific clan disciplines as the out of clan.<br /> <br /> As for how the first night went, he came to, and had no idea why he was so thirsty. It clicked though when a friend dropped by unexpectedly. He was lucky and barely managed to resist frenzy, but he did run out of there without any exploitation. Nice and awkward LOL. He called his regent who promptly flipped out because THIS SHOULDN'T BE POSSIBLE. She's a Carthian Gangrel so she doesn't know that about this kinda thing. So while he's waiting for her to arrive, this nice couple is walking down the street past him, and this time he fails his frenzy check and promptly mauls one of them while the other was trying to smack him off. His frenzy ended JUUUST before killing this guy, and he ran off. Unfortunately for him he made his humanity check, and left a massive masquerade breach, what with to live witnesses.<br /> <br /> He did manage to catch up to his regent/sire, and she remained ineffectual and had no idea who to even ask. So he suggested that this one woman from her childe's coterie might know something (she's a Mekhet Ordo Dracul, and PC). The Mekhet was able to figure out that he didn't have a clan, and he couldn't hold onto vitae. She pitched this like a good thing, being a bit of a mad scientist type. She said she'd try and help him with the blood thing, but he's not too optimistic right now! And that was how the first night went.<br /> <br /> I don't think he'll continue to luck out and not kill anyone, so this is gonna get much uglier =D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12572-electrographic","name":"Electrographic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T03:17:08-08:00","id":999646,"title":"","content":"If it's not a problem, i'd ask you to keep us informed; that first night as a Revenant was fun to read!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T07:35:10-08:00","id":999732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/990397-revenants-playing-as-one?p=999646#post999646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's not a problem, i'd ask you to keep us informed; that first night as a Revenant was fun to read!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I feel lie Revenants don't get a lot of attention (of course, that might be because there isn't much information on them yet).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T08:40:04-08:00","id":999772,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1349_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1349\" data-vbnamecard=\"1349\">Phersus</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12436_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12436\" data-vbnamecard=\"12436\">Ever Professional</a>. Sure, I'd be cool with writing more updates! I'm really glad you found that fun to read. We play an alternating weeks, so if updating at that frequency isn't thread necromancy, I'll be sure to add more!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12572-electrographic","name":"Electrographic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T08:45:45-08:00","id":999777,"title":"","content":"If we're expecting it, it's not necromancy. The thread's just in hibernation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T08:52:36-08:00","id":999779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/990397-revenants-playing-as-one?p=999777#post999777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we're expecting it, it's not necromancy. The thread's just in hibernation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome, thank you for letting me know! Alright then, I'll be sure to keep y'all up to date! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12572-electrographic","name":"Electrographic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T15:50:24-08:00","id":999997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Electrographic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/990397-revenants-playing-as-one?p=999779#post999779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright then, I'll be sure to keep y'all up to date! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yay! It is something i'<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">ve not saw in my games, so i'm interested. And that first night it was rough and visceral, just how i like them. Keep up the good work <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T23:38:15-08:00","id":1007060,"title":"","content":"Sorry to be late for the update, I had a pretty busy weekend! ANYWAY, I'd like warn y'all that unfortunately I did really well on all my frenzy checks despite not spending any will power &lt;/3<br /> <br /> Since I'm keeping you all updated I'll actually give the suckers names, and a bit of the main plot to help clear up my writing. My ghoul-turned-revenant is James. His regent/sire is Vixie, a Carthian Gangrel who's been around a while. We also the members of the cotorie James has been hanging around (read PCs), Tessa, a Mekhet in the Ordo Dracul; Draven, an unaligned Daeva; and the other two who might come up in later posts are Cam, Vixie's childe who's also a Carthian; Ivy, a Ventrue wanna-be Invictus. The main issue at hand is that our cotorie and all their sires blew the masquerade to the changelings in the city. The Invictus, who are in charge, are basically looking to arrest us all. I'm still gonna try to keep these posts focused on the Revenant issues as much as possible.<br /> <hr /><br /> As mentioned last time, right before the evening ended, Tessa managed to get 6 donated packets of blood (stolen from a hospital LOL) for James, so hopefully he wouldn't frenzy when he woke up the following night. Given that James's shitty little apartment is no Haven, he wound up moving some bedding into his closet and stuffed the cracks closed to keep the sunlight out. Super Classy. The real horror though was when he woke up the next evening. He was absolutely <i>drenched </i>in blood, and it basically looked like someone got murdered in his closet. He would have been really horrified by that if not for the fact he was pretty distracted by how unbelievably thirsty he was. He pretty much tore into the blood packs. Tessa had meant them to last a few days, but he went through the entire stock in one sitting. Even still, he was pretty thirsty (only 3 vitae!) but better able to access the whole OH MY GOD BLOOD EVERYWHERE! situation. A very ugly mess to clean up first thing in the evening &gt;:<br /> <br /> So after that he calls up Vixie to check in with her, and described what happened when he woke up and Vixie was like WOW THAT'S REALLY FUCKED UP I DON'T THINK I CAN HELP YOU WITH THIS ACTUALLY. Since Tessa had said the night before she wanted to have a talk with Vixie, James set up a meeting for all three of them in the back room of this bar later in the evening. James gets there first and about all he can notice it how easy it is to hear everyone's hearts beating with fresh, warm, beautiful blood. Still, he managed to maintain his composure until he got to the back room, though he just about chewed through his own lip. Vixie and Tessa both arrive and discuss some other pressing issues, and James gets a call from Draven, also regarding said issues. James brings up the whole I DIED thing and Draven pretty much goes OH THAT SUCKS. MAYBE VIXIE CAN HELP? (super helpful!) After that called wrapped up, Tessa decided that she'd take Vixie and James to see her sire (a coterie-mate of Vixie's, and also Ordo Dracul).<br /> <br /> On their way out of the back room, James and Tessa notice some Invictus vampires rolling up out front. Basically, because of issues mentioned above, they're here to arrest the three. Buuut the bar is full of so so many tasty blood filled people. Unfortunately, James still managed to hold off on frenzying right in the middle of the bar, though now he's really Tempted, so we'll see if that luck continues to hold out. James goes out the front to play hero/distraction, while the other two slip out the back. He managed to hold his own pretty well in a 4-v-1 fight but they ultimately subdue him, so now James is off to vampire jail on charges of breaching the masquerade!<br /> <hr /><br /> I WISH I WOULD FAIL ONE OF THESE FRENZY ROLLS. I thought for sure he'd have offed someone by accident at this point. Still, it's probably gonna cause some issues, since last they all checked, he was supposedly just a Ghoul. I'll keep you all posted until someone gets around to uplifting him.<br /> <br /> EDIT: My GM likes to give out extra Beats for out of character work like journals, or art, or whatever. I wrote a little <a href=\"http://tuxedoshark.tumblr.com/post/153363511461/how-its-gonna-be\" target=\"_blank\">perspective piece</a>, so I might as well toss it out here for for anyone who was curious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12572,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12572-electrographic","user":"Electrographic","date":".  Adding link to silly perspetive piece. 11-23-2016, 02:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12572-electrographic","name":"Electrographic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}